# CogniStream — AI-to-AI Payment Infrastructure
# Stack: Fastify + Prisma + PostgreSQL + Redis + TypeScript
## Architecture Rules
- Monorepo: /apps/api (Fastify), /apps/web (Next.js), /packages/shared (DTOs, types)
- Database: PostgreSQL 16 with Prisma ORM. NEVER raw SQL in business logic.
- All monetary values stored as INTEGER cents. NEVER float/decimal for money.
- All DB operations wrapped in transactions ($transaction) if touching balances.
- UUID v7 for all primary keys (time-sortable, index-friendly).
## Security Rules (CRITICAL)
- All inputs validated via Zod before hitting any service.
- API keys: store only bcrypt hashes. Original shown once on creation, never again.
- Rate limiting: per-org + per-agent + per-endpoint. Redis-backed sliding window.
- Escrow: atomic creation with transaction. No partial states allowed.
- No secrets in logs. No PII in logs. Sanitize all error messages.
## Code Quality
- Every service method needs unit test (Vitest) before PR.
- Integration tests for every endpoint that touches money.
- 80% coverage minimum for /apps/api.
- Conventional commits: feat|fix|docs|security|refactor(scope): message
## Performance
- DB queries: always select specific fields, never SELECT *.
- Redis caching for: agent profiles, reputation scores, rate limit windows.
- Kafka events for: transaction created, escrow released, reputation changed.
## Forbidden Patterns
- NO floating point for money.
- NO raw SQL strings.
- NO secrets in env files committed.
- NO console.log in production code (use Pino logger).
- NO auth bypass in tests (use mock JWT with explicit scopes).
